  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a larger container type is used to satisfy the demand of a smaller type, is the larger container counted as one unit of the smaller type's demand (i.e., one 12000 cm³ container fulfills one unit of type-1 demand), or is the substitution measured by volume so that the number of larger containers needed depends on the volume ratio between the two types?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how substitution is measured (unit count vs. volume ratio), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

